WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.460
Hi, I'm Freesia!

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.361
Modular's inference handbook prices memory and speed with simple formulas.

00:00:06.361 --> 00:00:07.921
Here's how they work.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.825
Every formula here is right.

00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:15.653
What matters is the input: a KV cache counts cached heads, not attention heads.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:20.704
Here's one token's cache, for Llama 3 8B.

00:00:21.124 --> 00:00:23.401
Thirty-two layers, each with its own cache.

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:29.875
Eight KV heads, not thirty-two attention heads: four query heads share each cached head.

00:00:30.295 --> 00:00:34.330
Head dimension one twenty-eight, two bytes each: about a hundred and thirty-one

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.675
thousand bytes a token.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.938
Qwen3-Next has forty-eight layers; only every fourth keeps a KV cache.

00:00:40.938 --> 00:00:43.086
The rest hold a fixed state.

00:00:43.506 --> 00:00:47.591
In those twelve, sixteen query heads share two cached heads: eight times

00:00:47.591 --> 00:00:49.293
smaller, then four times again.

00:00:49.713 --> 00:00:54.034
With attention heads, the handbook's calculator says a hundred and ninety-two gigabytes.

00:00:54.034 --> 00:00:55.834
The real cache is six.

00:00:57.217 --> 00:01:02.263
A draft model reads the context and guesses three tokens ahead: nice, today, outside.

00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:06.221
The target model checks all three in one pass, and keeps the

00:01:06.221 --> 00:01:07.696
longest prefix it agrees with.

00:01:08.116 --> 00:01:12.250
It keeps nice and today, rejects outside, and adds its own word, for.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.840
Three tokens for one pass.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.242
Servers log accepted over proposed: two thirds.

00:01:17.242 --> 00:01:22.355
Leviathan's formula wants something else: the chance each reached position is accepted.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:28.749
Fed that logged rate, the formula runs fifty-five percent low at seven drafted tokens.

00:01:32.517 --> 00:01:35.233
A formula is only as right as its input.

00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:38.553
Price the cache from KV heads, cached layers and cache type.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.486
To recap: count KV heads and cached layers, and know which

00:01:44.486 --> 00:01:45.790
acceptance rate you have.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.396
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:48.396 --> 00:01:49.020
I'm Freesia.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:49.332
Bye!
